{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1084986-what-s-up-with-fomarchs-and-with-book-of-the-wyrm-20-s-editing","id":1084986,"title":"What's up with Fomarchs? (and with Book of the Wyrm 20's editing)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-28T05:54:54-07:00","id":1084986,"title":"What's up with Fomarchs? (and with Book of the Wyrm 20's editing)","content":"The Fomarchs are stated in their description to all be passable as humans. Indeed, the text says that having the ability to conceal their appearance is indispensable to be considered a Fomarch. Like a super-Ferectoi.<br /> What are the three given Fomarh examples? A floating psychic jellyfish, a mutant psychic narwhal and a man/bat monstrosity who shrieks and spits acid. No reference to the ability to shapeshift is given.<br /> It's almost like they used two different authors to cover the same three-page material.<br /> Aside from that, the book is full, and I mean, full with incomplete sentences, syntax / spelling errors, repetitions and redundant sentences. Seriously... Was this book proofread at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T02:32:46-07:00","id":1085405,"title":"","content":"Yeah it was cringy editing, I like the bfook but a lot contradictions in some these books. I mean the Wendigo Uktena Sept in Africa, and Silver Fangs European Septs in China from World of Rage was also obvious mistakes.<br /> <br /> In the older editions were the Fomarchs supposed to be Humanoid or nonhumanoid? I first heard about them from Fomarol in 2nd ed Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T07:39:09-07:00","id":1085779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1084986-what-s-up-with-fomarchs-and-with-book-of-the-wyrm-20-s-editing?p=1085405#post1085405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah it was cringy editing, I like the bfook but a lot contradictions in some these books. I mean the Wendigo Uktena Sept in Africa, and Silver Fangs European Septs in China from World of Rage was also obvious mistakes.<br /> <br /> In the older editions were the Fomarchs supposed to be Humanoid or nonhumanoid? I first heard about them from Fomarol in 2nd ed Book of the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Freak Legion detailed them. They were basically short-lived generic monsters of several types that were used as raw materials for the old &quot;put Wyrm poisons in Pentex products!&quot; plot when they died. That particular avenue isn't an angle that the group uses in post-2nd edition presentations, though.","signatu